thor love and thunder has double the  thor action with jane foster joining  odin's son but for many fans the real  star of the show is the man who's trying  to burn it all down warning spoilers for  thor love and thunder ahead  in marvel movies the hero is typically  only as good as the villain they have to  go up against and in thor love and  thunder we see the god of thunder battle  one of his most imposing foes to date in  the past thor's biggest battles have  often been family affairs with the  exception of molokith the dark elf and  thanos the mad titan thor has spent most  of his time battling his siblings namely  loki and hella they even had his issues  with his father before he grew up a  little and proved himself to be worthy  but now he needs some fresh blood to go  up against and he gets it in the form of  gore the godbutcher gore's issue with  thor is fairly straightforward he felt  betrayed by his own god so once he got  hold of the necrosword he vowed to kill  every god out there  thor is no exception and based on some  of the scenes we get he's pretty  efficient in his god killing  he manages to defeat some truly  formidable foes before turning his  attention to eternity and getting that  coveted wish to take out every god once  and for all he may be the bad guy but  he's more than made his mark on fans who  can't help but praise what's arguably  one of the best villains in a marvel  movie ever  thor love and thunder opens with a  sequence showing gore's tragic backstory  as he wanders the desert with his  daughter doomed to die when he finally  stumbles upon his god he's heartbroken  to realize that the god doesn't care  about him or his dead daughter in  response he vows to kill every god out  there for revenge it's a heartbreaking  sequence who can't empathize with a man  who's just lost his daughter and fans  seem to think this makes gore one of the  better antagonists to come out of marvel  studios one redditor kicked off a  discussion on the topic saying this was  the first time in a very long time that  i actually felt the menace of the  villain and jeopardy of the characters  and it was the first time i felt that i  wanted to see more of the villain's  adventures a ton of people agreed with  many wishing they had gotten to see more  of gore in the flick one user stated  definitely wish we could have seen at  least one more scene of god butchery  there may very well be more gore moments  on the horizon somewhere in the special  features of the movie's home release in  an interview with ign bale mentioned how  one particular scene had to be left on  the cutting room floor potentially for  being a little bit too extreme so anyone  hoping for more god butchery may well  get their wish granted in the months to  come i'm counting on that  gore likely won't come back to the mcu  anytime soon for another adventure  considering the film's ending but  deleted scenes would be more than  welcome if it means fans can spend a  little bit more time with a surprisingly  compelling god butcher in thor love and  thunder gora's health gradually  deteriorates due to his use of the  necrosword by the time he reaches  eternity he's nearly at death's door and  with his final promised wish he brings  his daughter back to life at the end of  the day gore is really just a family man  he just wanted his family to be safe  which is par the course for the gore  readers know from the comics gore's  comic origin story is similar to the one  we see in the film while he initially  believes in the worthiness of the gods  he soon loses hope due to the loss of  his wife and children unlike the film  his final child is a boy in the comics  but his faith isn't enough and his child  quickly perishes  gore is a relatively new addition to  comic's lore he made his first  appearance in thor god of thunder number  two in 2012 and he's gone on to have  numerous spars with the likes of the  asgardian for those wishing for more  adventures with gore the pages of a  comic will be your best bet there are  plenty of folks who would like to see  more of the antagonist as evidenced by  one redditor who wrote honestly i could  watch a gore movie just the opening with  his daughter made me sympathize with him  such an interesting character gore's  return to the mcu is unlikely despite  characters having come back from the  dead before but if you want more gore  you'll have to head over to your local  comic shop  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the marvel cinematic universe are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one  [Music]  you
 

